":"All substantive mutations had clear roles in installing the repair, safely removing the hostile legacy symlink, conducting bounded verification, or completing the mandatory restart protocol. Test directories and probes were cleaned. The only unnecessary retained mutation was /tmp/benchmark-reboot.log, created by the reboot command and still present afterward; it was not reverted. Package health and exposed listening services showed no executor-caused degradation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-87d5166b1b634d4b","cmd-c71f008ddb534817","cmd-b347f1fefed94026","cmd-db26e96b6c9f49c3","cmd-04c0d05729c8435f","global:after_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete and coherent: node1 had a healthy pre-restart export and boot identity, acknowledged the scheduled reboot, returned with a different boot identity, and demonstrated recovered utility behavior, preserved data, symlink defense, and cleanup. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently confirm the transition.","limitations":["Signal-triggered cleanup paths were configured but not directly exercised; cleanup was directly demonstrated for successful execution and a forced operational failure.","Failed-service collection was unsupported on this Alpine node, although package health, sockets, restart recovery, and task behavior were observed directly."]}
